{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And He gave to Moses, when He had finished.</b> After Scripture recounted what good was attained at the conclusion of all the forty days that Moses spent on the mountain, it explains the reason why the end that the blessed El had designated in the giving of the Torah was not attained — He having said, וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי מַמְלֶכֶת כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ (Exodus 19:6), and having said, מִזְבַּח אֲדָמָה תַּעֲשֶׂה לִּי בְּכָל הַמָּקוֹם אָבֹא אֵלֶיךָ (Exodus 20:21) — until it became necessary to make the Mishkan. And He informed that this came about because of the evil choice of Israel. For truly, at the end of the first forty days, He gave the tablets, the work of Elohim, to sanctify all of them as priests and a holy nation, according to all His good word. But they rebelled and corrupted their way and fell from their excellence, as He testified in saying, וַיִּתְנַצְּלוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת עֶדְיָם מֵהַר חוֹרֵב (Exodus 33:6)." "<b>The two tablets of the testimony.</b> Those which He testified He would give in saying, וְאֶתְּנָה לְךָ אֶת לֻחֹת הָאֶבֶן (Exodus 24:12). But before He gave the Torah and the commandment that He wrote, as He had testified, they began the act of the calf, and He said to Moses, לֶךְ רֵד כִּי שִׁחֵת עַמְּךָ (Exodus 32:7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:45.280298630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}